With per-branch coverage high, CRAP ≈ cyclomatic complexity here, so the function's decision points (`typeof` check, `try/catch`, two `parsed && Array.isArray(...)` guards, final `Array.isArray`) push CC to 9. Collapse the branches to get CC ≤ 7:

```javascript
function _parseWorkflowRunJobs(raw) {
    var parsed = raw;
    if (typeof parsed === 'string') {
        try { parsed = JSON.parse(parsed); } catch (e) { return []; }
    }
    if (!parsed || typeof parsed !== 'object') return [];
    if (!Array.isArray(parsed)) parsed = parsed.jobs || parsed.job_runs;
    return Array.isArray(parsed) ? parsed : [];
}
```

Even better: drop this function entirely and export/reuse the identical `js/common/ci.js::_jobsOf` (see the adjacent suggestion) — that both fixes the gate and removes the duplication. Note `detectFailedChecks` itself improved (86.9 → 74.6), so this new helper is the only gate blocker.
